# Example per-device ACL for netsocket's Mosquitto broker.
# Enable it from mosquitto.conf (`acl_file /mosquitto/config/acl`) together
# with `allow_anonymous false` and a `password_file`.
#
# Convention: each device authenticates with its own username equal to its
# device id (e.g. `c3-a4cf12ab34`), and %u expands to that username.

# The netsocket server needs to see discovery and all device state.
user netsocket-server
topic readwrite #

# Bespoke devices: full access to their own subtree only.
user c3-a4cf12ab34
topic readwrite netsocket/dev/c3-a4cf12ab34/#

# Repeat per device. Zigbee2MQTT has its own broker user with access to
# zigbee2mqtt/# and homeassistant/# on the Z2M config side.